WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.050
There are five tabs across the top: My dates, Tasks, Supplies, Contractors, and Help. Here's what each one does for you.

2
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:15.190
The page says hello by name, and each tab starts with a short welcome and three quick steps.

3
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.290
Let's start with My dates. This is where you choose the days you'd like to work at La Maison.

4
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:25.410
The yellow box lists the three steps to sign up. Here's how each one looks.

5
00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.710
Every date gets its own card. A grey card with a lock means someone already has that day.

6
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:37.030
The card also shows the cleaner and the inspector for that day, so you know who you're working with.

7
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:44.070
A white card with an empty box is open for you. The word Needed means that job is still available.

8
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.710
Each card gives you the date, the hours, and who else is working that day.

9
00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.750
Some cards say same-day turnover, right next to the hours.

10
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.330
And some cards show only the checkout time, like this one.

11
00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:01.470
The dates run in order, soonest first. Keep scrolling to see the months ahead.

12
00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:06.150
Found a day you like? Tap the card. The box fills in with a check mark.

13
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.590
Pick as many dates as you want, all in one visit.

14
00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:16.390
Now the important part: tap Sign me up. That tap puts your name on the La Maison calendar.

15
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:22.730
A check mark alone doesn't save your spot. If you leave without tapping Sign me up, the date stays open.

16
00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:28.610
The Sign me up button waits at the bottom of the screen. It turns dark blue once you've changed a date.

17
00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:34.150
Once you're signed up, your name shows on that day's calendar event, from checkout to check-in.

18
00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.130
You'll also see a calendar with all of your dates on it.

19
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:44.130
Plans change, and that's fine. Uncheck the date, tap Sign me up again, and it opens up for someone else.

20
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.150
Inspectors, your link works the same way, with inspections in place of cleanings.

21
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:54.930
Your white cards are the dates that still need an inspection. You can also see who's cleaning that day.

22
00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.730
Cleaners and inspectors sign up separately, so one date can have both of you on it.

23
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:05.570
Next up, the Tasks tab. Inspectors, this is your checklist for every visit.

24
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:12.090
The welcome box sums it up: open each area of the house, check off every item, then tap Submit.

25
00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.450
Please go through the whole list every time, even if the house looked great last visit.

26
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:24.070
There are 76 items, sorted into 13 areas like Bathroom, Kitchen, and Living Areas.

27
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:29.150
Tap an area to open it. The numbers on the right keep track of how far you've gotten.

28
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:34.950
Each item is one small thing to check, like placing toilet paper in the cabinets over the toilets.

29
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.050
Finished an item? Tap the box next to it.

30
00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:44.270
Curious why an item is on the list? Tap Instructions and why it matters for the reason behind it.

31
00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.740
Finished items get a check mark and a line through them, and your count goes up.

32
00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:52.710
Tapped one by mistake? Tap it again to uncheck it.

33
00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:59.390
Then move on to the next area. The Kitchen has 10 items, from the coffee to the pots and pans.

34
00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:03.070
At the bottom, you can see how many items you've completed.

35
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.930
All done? Tap Submit inspection, and your results are on their way to us.

36
00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:12.410
If you see a Your name box above the button, type your name first.

37
00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:16.810
Running low on something at the house? That's what the Supplies tab is for.

38
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:23.230
It's three steps again: pick the item, say how much is left, and tap Add Item to List.

39
00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:26.830
Tap the first box to open the list of items the house uses.

40
00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:32.190
Or start typing. Type paper, and you'll see paper towels and toilet paper.

41
00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.890
Can't find it? You can add what you typed as a new item.

42
00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:40.430
Then say how much is left, like 2 rolls or half a bottle.

43
00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.430
Tap Add Item to List, and we'll restock it.

44
00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:49.150
Need the pool service or a plumber? The Contractors tab has La Maison's maintenance vendors.

45
00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:53.170
Find the contractor you need, then tap to text or email them.

46
00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.910
The search box finds a vendor by name, type, phone, or email.

47
00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:01.930
Type pool, for example, and the pool service comes right up.

48
00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.830
Tap Text or Email to reach them directly.

49
00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:10.430
If a vendor has no email on file, the Email button is faded, so send a text.

50
00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.590
And if you ever forget a step, the Help tab has it all in writing.

51
00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:22.770
It covers the whole visit: pick your dates, get on the calendar, then use Tasks, Supplies, and Contractors on the day.

52
00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:27.920
That's everything. Thank you for taking such good care of La Maison.

